# Environment lookups a native library makes are --wrap'd onto Env.c so a variable
# the GUEST set at run time is visible. One name per line; '#' comments ignored.
#
# Only the read side is wrapped. A native setenv writes the host's vector, which the
# guest does not read back, but nothing in the libraries ported so far does that and
# a write bridge needs a policy for who owns a name.
getenv
secure_getenv
